{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>He who plants</b> — a participle, like: \"who spreads out the earth.\" Because of the gutteral letter [in the root], and this interpretation is weighty, for eyes and ears have no need, for it is He who gives power to eyes to see and to ears to hear. Behold, sight and hearing are from Him — so how would He not know everything?! And he mentioned the ears first, because he completed [the phrase] and did not follow the pattern of: \"and I gave it to Esau.\" And he mentioned planting with the ears, for they are planted like the two points of the poles [of the sphere] in the firmament, and with the eye he mentioned forming, for forms are continually formed in the eye."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 94, :notes {0 "The phrase כדרך: ואתן לעשו appears to cite Genesis 36:8 ויתן לעשו as a grammatical parallel for word order; rendered literally as cited. The word הסדנים (poles/axles of a celestial sphere) is a technical astronomy term; translated accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:13.218966940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}